  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "friKFr5snjS82jD5P+6oFulD3O8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:50.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The import that matters\n\n```ts\nimport { createRemoteAttachmentService } from \"@powerhousedao/reactor-attachments/client\";\n```\n\nPoint it at the same Switchboard the light client uses, then pass it in:\n\n```tsx\n<GraphQLReactorProvider url={switchboardUrl} attachmentService={attachmentService}>\n  <YourApp />\n</GraphQLReactorProvider>\n```\n\nImport the **`/client` subpath, not the package root**. The root entry also exports the Kysely, S3 and filesystem backends, so a browser bundler has to resolve `kysely`, `@aws-sdk/client-s3` and `node:fs` \u2014 and fails before any app code runs. This is the same failure class as importing `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser` from its root instead of `/graphql-client`, and it has the same shape of fix: import the browser subpath.\n\n## Who owns what\n\nAttachments are configured at the same point as everything else, but the **app constructs the service**. Which storage it talks to is the app's business; `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser` does not depend on the attachment implementation at all.\n\nThe provider publishes the service into the `window.ph.attachmentService` slot Connect publishes it into, so `useAttachmentService` and the editors below find it. Leave the prop out and the slot stays empty, exactly as it is without the provider.\n\nIt is published from its **own effect, keyed on the prop**, so an app that builds the service asynchronously can pass it in later \u2014 passing a new service does not rebuild the client or the document cache.\n\n## Honest caveat\n\nThe docs are explicit that this prop is a **wiring seam and nothing more has been proven**: the service an app passes reaches `useAttachmentService` below the provider, but no attachment has been read over the light client end to end. Treat a working attachment flow on this client as something to verify yourself rather than assume.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/08-ReactorBrowserClient/03-SubgraphsAndAttachments.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:50.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:50.000Z"
    }
  },
